Title: 1.x Subscriber receives value after unsubscription
Description: Is it expected that this test case fails?

Or the OnSubscribe is incomplete with this design (missing explicit `isUnsubscribed()` check)?

```
@Test
public void testAfterUnsubscribeNoValue() throws InterruptedException {
    TestSubscriber<String> ts = new TestSubscriber<>();
    AtomicBoolean unsubscribed = new AtomicBoolean();
    CountDownLatch latch = new CountDownLatch(2);

    Observable<String> s1 = Observable.create(s -> {

        Thread t = new Thread(() -> {
            try {
                Thread.sleep(1000);
                s.onNext("should not be displayed");
                latch.countDown();
            } catch (InterruptedException ignored) {
            }
        });

        s.add(Subscriptions.create(() -> {
            unsubscribed.set(true);
            latch.countDown();
        }));
        t.start();
    });

    Subscription subscription = s1.subscribe(ts);
    subscription.unsubscribe();

    if (latch.await(2000, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS)) {
        ts.assertNoValues();
        assertTrue(unsubscribed.get());
        assertTrue(subscription.isUnsubscribed());
    } else {
        fail("timed out waiting for latch");
    }
}
```


